{"version":"1","source":"Architectural Atlas procedural model","scope":"St Basil's Cathedral, Moscow (simplified schematic)","title":"St Basil's Cathedral","location":"Moscow, Russia","blurb":"The Cathedral of the Intercession on Red Square, built 1555 to 1561 for Ivan the Terrible, in simplified schematic form: nine chapels on one foundation around the tent-roofed central church, each with its onion dome.","sourceUrls":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Saint Basil’s Cathedral","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Basil%27s_Cathedral"},{"label":"uvisitrussia.com: interview with the Pokrovsky Cathedral chief curator","url":"https://www.uvisitrussia.com/news/saint-basils-cathedral-moscow.html"}],"systems":[{"id":"foundations","name":"Basement platform","color":"#b0a58a","description":"The single basement foundation platform carrying all nine chapels."},{"id":"central-church","name":"Church of the Intercession","color":"#e8ddc9","description":"The central octagonal Church of the Intercession with its tent roof and gilded onion dome."},{"id":"cardinal-chapels","name":"Cardinal chapels","color":"#e8ddc9","description":"The four larger octagonal side churches on the compass points, each with its own onion dome."},{"id":"diagonal-chapels","name":"Diagonal chapels","color":"#e8ddc9","description":"The four smaller cuboid side churches on the diagonals, each with its own onion dome."},{"id":"st-basil-chapel","name":"Chapel of St Basil","color":"#1f7a4d","description":"The tenth chapel, added in 1588 over the grave of St Basil the Blessed."},{"id":"gallery","name":"Gallery and porches","color":"#d9cfae","description":"The vaulted connecting gallery and entrance porches linking the chapels."}],"explanations":{"basement platform":"The single basement foundation on which all nine chapels stand, covering about 1,680 sq m. Exact platform form is schematic.","central church lower tier":"The lower octagonal tier of the central Church of the Intercession. Exact tier heights are schematic.","central church upper tier":"The upper octagonal tier of the central church, 46 m tall inside with a floor of only 64 sq m. Exact tier heights are schematic.","central tent roof":"The tent (shatyor) roof of the central church, the towering octagonal pyramid at the heart of the composition. Exact pitch is schematic.","central onion dome":"The small gilded onion dome crowning the central tent. Dome colors are schematic.","central cross":"The cross atop the central church, reaching 47.5 m: the cathedral was Moscow’s tallest building until the Ivan the Great Bell Tower overtook it in 1600. Exact cross form is schematic.","central kokoshniki":"The kokoshnik gables ringing the central church: decorative arched gables typical of Russian church architecture. Exact count and shapes are schematic.","north chapel":"The north side church, one of the four larger octagonal chapels on the compass points, with its onion dome and cross. Exact size and colors are schematic.","north chapel kokoshniki":"The kokoshnik gables of the north chapel. Exact count and shapes are schematic.","south chapel":"The south side church with its onion dome and cross. Exact size and colors are schematic.","south chapel kokoshniki":"The kokoshnik gables of the south chapel. Exact count and shapes are schematic.","east chapel":"The east side church with its onion dome and cross. Exact size and colors are schematic.","east chapel kokoshniki":"The kokoshnik gables of the east chapel. Exact count and shapes are schematic.","west chapel":"The west side church with its onion dome and cross. Exact size and colors are schematic.","west chapel kokoshniki":"The kokoshnik gables of the west chapel. Exact count and shapes are schematic.","northeast chapel":"The northeast side church, one of the four smaller cuboid diagonal chapels. Exact size and colors are schematic.","northeast chapel kokoshniki":"The kokoshnik gables of the northeast chapel. Exact count and shapes are schematic.","northwest chapel":"The northwes